-- ex35 two-habitats table, rank-1 rows plus the 3x2 lattice rows: generator, reduce, scan, grade, shift. Twin of 35-two-habitats.bqn.
-- Split -a..-e by fixture: the .bqn's per-row scratch worlds carry different n (5/4/8/3) and lattice shapes (2x3/4x4), so one registry cannot hold them all; this file is the n-5 world with the 2-row-by-3-column fields (elevation, cost, safety, g), registry lattice 3 2 (w h).
-- Table spellings adapted to runnable forms where the schematic row does not parse against this fixture:
--   scan row `+\ Damage @ graded` is written scan(+) Damage along (grade Damage): the graded-view scan; the .bqn asserts the value-order result only, never a scatter-back.
--   grade rows `top 5 (grade Threat)` / `top 8 (grade Safety @ 64 64)` are pinned at the .bqn's k and grade direction: top 3 (grade desc Threat), top 2 (grade desc Safety @ 3 2).
--   space scopes say 3 2 where the table says 64 64: the fixture's own shape.
--   the rank-2 generator (↕ w‿h) has no query surface; its assertion stays in the .bqn twin.
--! registry ../registries/35-two-habitats-a.reg
--! expect g = 0 0 0 1 2 3

-- generator: the ground is minted by iota, rank 1
--! out 0 1 2 3 4
↕5

-- reduce: scoped fold to one scalar, both habitats
--! out 42
+/ Gold @ Nord
--! out 21
+/ Elevation @ 3 2

-- scan: entities scan along the graded view, space scans in lattice order
--! out 1 3 6 10 15
scan(+) Damage along (grade Damage)
--! out 1 1 1 2 2 2
+\ Cost @ 3 2

-- grade: top k by grading down (indices, descending value)
--! out 1 3 4
top 3 (grade desc Threat)
--! out 5 4
top 2 (grade desc Safety @ 3 2)

-- shift: prev is a parallel shift with fill, never an order-carried recurrence (decision record)
--! out 0 5 8 13 21
prev.X
-- rank-2 prev shifts a whole zero ROW in along the leading axis: 1 2 3 / 4 5 6 becomes 0 0 0 / 1 2 3
3 2 , G = prev.G
